{"step_index":1042,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-11T23:26:50Z","thinking":"**Assessing the Resource Exhaustion**\n\nThe subagent orchestrator encountered repeated resource exhaustion errors (429). The PIPELINE SENTINEL has complete control, including execution commands. Direct verification of the conjecture is now possible.\n\n\n**Investigating Potential Counterexamples**\n\nThe exhaustive tests and mathematical reasoning suggest the inequality might hold, but the possibility of a large-diameter counterexample warrants investigation. Focusing on graphs where diameter is less than or equal to twice the radius minus two is the key. Generating and testing all connected graphs on 7 and 8 vertices seems feasible, given the manageable number of such graphs.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"\"/mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/.venv/bin/python -c '\\nimport networkx as nx\\n\\n# networkx has graph_atlas_g() which contains all non-isomorphic graphs up to 7 vertices!\\natlas = nx.graph_atlas_g()\\nprint(f\\\"Atlas contains {len(atlas)} graphs.\\\")\\n\\ndef roman_domination(G):\\n    # compute exact roman domination using ILP with scipy or networkx or pulp\\n    # min sum(x_v + 2*y_v)\\n    # s.t. x_v + y_v + sum_{u in N(v)} y_u >= 1\\n    # x_v + y_v <= 1\\n    import pulp\\n    prob = pulp.LpProblem(\\\"Roman\\\", pulp.LpMinimize)\\n    nodes = list(G.nodes())\\n    x = {v: pulp.LpVariable(f\\\"x_{v}\\\", cat=\\\"Binary\\\") for v in nodes}\\n    y = {v: pulp.LpVariable(f\\\"y_{v}\\\", cat=\\\"Binary\\\") for v in nodes}\\n    prob += pulp.lpSum(x[v] + 2*y[v] for v in nodes)\\n    for v in nodes:\\n        prob += x[v] + y[v] + pulp.lpSum(y[u] for u in G.neighbors(v)) >= 1\\n        prob += x[v] + y[v] <= 1\\n    prob.solve(pulp.PULP_CBC_CMD(msg=0))\\n    return int(pulp.value(prob.objective))\\n\\nn_checked = 0\\nfor G in atlas:\\n    if G.number_of_nodes() < 2: continue\\n    if not nx.is_connected(G): continue\\n    n_checked += 1\\n    rad = nx.radius(G)\\n    rom = roman_domination(G)\\n    if rad + 1 > rom:\\n        print(f\\\"COUNTEREXAMPLE FOUND in atlas! n={G.number_of_nodes()}, edges={list(G.edges())}, rad={rad}, rom={rom}\\\")\\n        exit(0)\\n\\nprint(f\\\"All {n_checked} connected graphs in Atlas (up to n=7) checked. ZERO COUNTEREXAMPLES!\\\")\\n'\"","Cwd":"\"/mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/handoff/promising13/task_e20263a9\"","WaitMsBeforeAsync":"5000","toolAction":"\"Checking all graphs in graph atlas up to n=7\"","toolSummary":"\"Check graph atlas up to n=7\""}}]}
