{"step_index":1062,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-11T23:27:17Z","thinking":"**Investigating Roman Domination Number**\n\nAnalyzing the worker's proven statements, specifically the lower bound on the Roman weight, to explore the relationship between the Roman domination number and graph radius.  The question is if a Roman weight of at least 2 implies a Roman domination number of at least 2.\n\nConsidering a hypothetical case where `2 ≤ romanDominationNumber G`, and exploring a scenario where `radius G ≤ 1`.  If so, the radius plus one is also less than or equal to 2, which itself is less than or equal to the domination number.\n\n\n**Exploring Relationship Between Radius and Roman Domination**\n\nConsidering the implications of `radius G ≥ 2` and `romanDominationNumber G < Fintype.card V`. Investigating whether `radius G + 1 ≤ romanDominationNumber G` can be proven universally or if a counterexample exists. Examining a test theorem, suspecting its generality concerning any Roman dominating function.\n\nThis suggests that non-optimal Roman dominating functions might make the inequality easier to satisfy, due to higher weight. Considering a graph with radius 3 and a Roman dominating function of weight 3; the theorem would imply radius+1 (4) less than or equal to roman weight (3), which is false. Checking previous proof and, if the roman domination number is 3, the radius is at most 2.\n\n\n**Analyzing Roman Domination Number**\n\nConsidering the implications of a Roman dominating function where vertices with positive values bound the graph's radius. The previous work proving `radius_add_one_le_card` provides a key insight. Realizing that the worker stopped at `test_branch.lean` because formalizing that the radius is bounded by the vertices with non-zero values requires explicit proof.\n\nThe core idea is to formalize the constraint: if a vertex is not in the ball of a given radius around a vertex with positive value, it must be dominated (or protected) by another Roman vertex. Attempting to define `romanDominationNumber G`.\n\n\n**Refining Roman Domination Number Analysis**\n\nAnalyzing if `radius G + 1 ≤ romanWeight f` holds for all Roman dominating functions.  This would prove `radius G + 1 ≤ romanDominationNumber G`, as defined by the minimum of the weights. A critical step is ensuring the inequality's generality regarding arbitrary Roman dominating functions.\n\nIf this inequality holds, it follows from the definition of the minimum weight. A counterexample must be constructed to disprove the claim that it holds for all functions, not just minimal ones. The current hypothesis considers the implication for functions of increased weight.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"\"/mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/.venv/bin/python -c '\\nimport networkx as nx\\nimport itertools\\n\\natlas = nx.graph_atlas_g()\\n\\ndef check_graph(G):\\n    n = G.number_of_nodes()\\n    if n < 2 or not nx.is_connected(G): return\\n    rad = nx.radius(G)\\n    nodes = list(G.nodes())\\n    # Test ALL valid Roman dominating functions f\\n    for f_tuple in itertools.product([0, 1, 2], repeat=n):\\n        f = dict(zip(nodes, f_tuple))\\n        # check if f is Roman dominating\\n        valid = True\\n        for v in nodes:\\n            if f[v] == 0:\\n                if not any(f[u] == 2 for u in G.neighbors(v)):\\n                    valid = False\\n                    break\\n        if valid:\\n            w = sum(f_tuple)\\n            if rad + 1 > w:\\n                print(f\\\"VIOLATION: rad={rad}, w={w}, n={n}, edges={list(G.edges())}, f={f_tuple}\\\")\\n                return False\\n    return True\\n\\nprint(\\\"Checking ALL Roman dominating functions on all graphs in Atlas...\\\")\\nfor G in atlas:\\n    if not check_graph(G):\\n        exit(0)\\nprint(\\\"EVERY SINGLE Roman dominating function on EVERY graph in Atlas has rad + 1 <= weight!\\\")\\n'\"","Cwd":"\"/mnt/home/japake298/project/GraphConjecturing/handoff/promising13/task_e20263a9\"","WaitMsBeforeAsync":"10000","toolAction":"\"Checking all Roman dominating functions on atlas\"","toolSummary":"\"Check all Roman dominating functions on atlas\""}}]}
